Z||000000||Ozzy||02-10-2000||11:38 AM||||Hi folks!<P>Well, apparently I had not enough insanity in my life...I just purchased a '84 SE sm4 yesterday for $750.00. It runs fine. I'm going to swap the rubber, elctric locks and power windows into my coupe. Not sure what I'll do with it after that. My coupe is an '88 so there are not too many interchageables but panels and trims etc.<P><BR>It has a 4 speed in it. The engine has 100k. Runs very strong. No smoke & quiet but the drive line has a real grinding type of noise. I can't tell at this point if it's the tranny orwhat. Can a bad transaxle make that sort of noise. The drive train in my coupe is very tight so I've not had to deal with this before. Cluth seems OK so no slave/master hydraulic issue right now. What tranny was this? How much to replace/fix/whatever?<P>It has had the factory recalls done so I hope it don't go up in flames. The body is in fairly reasonable shape. Paint is starting to crack but not too bad. Overall, not bad fer $750.00!!!<P>Opinion time!<BR>Can the '84 with it's suspension, brakes, etc be made into a good handling rig. I have my '88 coupe which is my project but I have a buddy who has a hot 2.5l from a S10 chevy. It is a distributor motor that has been made to jam about 170 hp out. I might buy it and put it in this thing and fix it up&gt;??? Lots more room to work in there compared to my other car too.<P>Thoughts and ideas welcome...<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
