Z||000003||kidzwheelz||02-11-2000||08:22 AM||||  Call 1-800-pmcares , and just give them your VIN number!||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||02-11-2000||09:50 AM||||Did you check the fluid level in the tranny?<BR>Also look for leaks while your at it.  Its possible the fluid is a bit low, and you may have gotten a better deal than you think.<P>You also might check to make sure that the brakes arent dragging, and that there is not anything caught in those areas.  Make sure the stone shield that protects the back of the brake rotors is not get bent enough to touch the rotor.  I had this happen after working on an engine.  It was a frustrating problem to track down.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ozzy||02-11-2000||11:36 AM||||Hi Folks...Brain Fart! 2m4 not sm4! brb.<P>Anyhow, no I did not check the fluid level but there is a seal leaking. If that is the problem that would be nice but I suspect it has been that way for awhile. Significant backlash now.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||02-13-2000||03:12 AM||||C,mon guys... Still need some transmission info on this '84 2m4, 4 spd. Who made it? Can I buy parts for it or should it be rebuilt? <P><BR>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||02-13-2000||08:53 AM||||Ozzy, I think all the 4 speeds are Muncies, but many of the 84 models had the lower gear ratio trannies (4:11). Many people like this tranny because of the quicker acceleration (but it does cut down on the top end a little). Don't know about parts availability, but a transmission shop should be able to tell you. Rodney Dickman is a tranny expert, give him a call.<P>I don't know about the 2.5 engines, but the V6 engines are different for the rear wheel drive vehicles (like the S-10). Fieros use front wheel drive engines. Check to see if that S-10 has the starter on the same side as your Fiero, if not, it will require a bunch of modifying to get it to fit.<P>87 Steve GT, I don't think you can get recall info from that 1-800-PMCARES number anymore. Call the local Pontiac dealer with your VIN and they can check the computer to see if it has any outstanding recalls.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Trixi||02-14-2000||02:47 PM||||hi<BR>i have an 84 se, my trannie was grinding when i shifted it cost me $1800 for a used trannie and new racing clutch the trannie is a 4 spd munchie this included trans, clutch, and labour aprox 2 days in the shop||||reg||1
